    {# Meet Naming Convention #}
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Entering Meet Info</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">The name of a meet you are hosting must follow this format:</p>
      <div class="mt-3 rounded-lg bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-slate-800">
        YEAR-Month-Day (Your Gym Short Name) (Local or Invite) (Levels)
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600"><strong>Example:</strong> <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">2021-10-15 CT-NewEra Local 4-6 &amp; XCEL</code></p>
    </div>

    {# Gym Info Note #}
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-slate-950">Gym Information</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700">The most important thing is that the <strong>short name MUST BE correct</strong>. There are <strong>NO SPACES</strong> in short names. The official name should be the name on the website. The rest of the info is up to you, but copying the info from the CT website would be wise.</p>
    </div>

